posts.body:
The
actor
method of
Window_BattleActor
is designed differently in MZ:
In MV, it is called with no arguments, and returns the currently-selected actor.
In MZ, it expects to be given an index, and returns the actor at that index.
You could try a small patch like this (untested):
JavaScript:
/*:
 * @target MZ
 * @plugindesc FOSSIL extension: Window_BattleStatus#actor.
 * @author Caethyril
 * @url https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/threads/171623/
 * @orderAfter YEP_BattleEngineCore
 * @help Free to use and/or modify for any project, no credit required.
 */
;void (alias => {
  Window_BattleStatus.prototype.actor = function(index, ...args) {
    if (index === undefined)
      return alias.call(this, this.index(), ...args);
    return alias.apply(this, arguments);
  };
})(Window_BattleStatus.prototype.actor);
